111	// flattenExisting flattens a checkpoint's current subtree into a path->entry map
112	// keyed under basePath, so the per-checkpoint write helpers (which build paths as
113	// basePath+"<n>/<file>") see the existing files. basePath is "" for the
114	// per-checkpoint-ref layout or "<shard>/<id>/" for the v1 branch layout. A nil
115	// subtree (new checkpoint) yields an empty map.
